<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Project Hub</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, shrink-to-fit=no">
  <link href="https://stackpath.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/4.2.1/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
</head>

<body>
  <!-- Navigation (same as your other pages) -->
  <nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-dark bg-dark static-top">
    <ul class="navbar-nav">
      <li class="nav-item active">
        <a class="nav-link" href="/">Home</a>
      </li>
      <li class="nav-item">
        <a class="nav-link" href="/projects">Projects</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <!-- WELCOME HEADER -->
  <header class="jumbotron jumbotron-fluid bg-light text-dark mb-0">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <h1 class="display-4">Welcome to Jacob’s Project Hub</h1>
      <p class="lead">A simple DevOps playground—download, demo, and track your builds in one place.</p>
      <a href="/projects" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Browse Projects</a>
    </div>
  </header>
  
  <!-- ABOUT ME SECTION -->
  <section id="about" class="py-5 bg-white">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>About the Creator</h2>
      <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-4 text-center mb-4">
          <img src="/images/profile.jpg" class="rounded-circle img-fluid" alt="Jacob Baker">
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-8">
          <p>Hi, I’m Jacob Baker. As a Computer Science student and Web Service Director, I built Project Hub to streamline how my team shares pre-release builds. I tackled real‑world DevOps challenges—managing temp files, logging downloads, and running executables on demand—all in a single, easy‑to‑use page.</p>
          <p>With rock‑solid Node.js/Express back‑end and EJS templating, plus Bootstrap styling, Project Hub reflects my passion for clean, practical tools that boost productivity.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROJECT DETAILS SECTION -->
  <section id="project-details" class="py-5 bg-light">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What Project Hub Does</h2>
      <p>Project Hub simplifies build distribution by offering:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>One‑Click Download:</strong> Grab the latest ZIP or EXE without hunting through folders.</li>
        <li><strong>Temporary File Handling:</strong> Copies each build to a temp directory, so you always serve a fresh, isolated file.</li>
        <li><strong>Download History:</strong> Logs every download in <code>history.txt</code> with timestamps for audit trails.</li>
        <li><strong>Server‑Side Execution:</strong> Spin up builds on the server via a dedicated endpoint for quick demos.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Designed for small teams and solo developers, it’s the perfect starting point for more advanced features like authentication, multi‑project support, or CI/CD integration.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FOOTER -->
  <footer class="mt-auto bg-dark text-light py-3">
    <div class="container text-center">
      &copy; 2025 Jacob Baker. All rights reserved.
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script src="/js/jquery.min.js"></script>
  <script src="/js/bootstrap.min.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
